# Files carried into every worktree Claude Code creates for this repository.
#
# The runtime copies listed paths file by file and SKIPS SYMLINKS — it logs
# "Skipping symlink in .worktreeinclude" and moves on. site/node_modules holds 17
# symlinks, so listing it here produced a node_modules that arrived incomplete and
# could not build, while looking as though it had worked. Run `npm ci` inside the
# worktree instead; it is slower and it is correct.
#
# .foundry/ needs no entry: its memory, runbooks and config are committed, so a
# worktree gets them from git. Two consequences worth knowing before dispatching
# agents with `isolation: worktree`:
#   - .foundry/blackboard/ is gitignored, so it does NOT exist in a fresh worktree
#     and anything written there is invisible to the main checkout and to sibling
#     agents. An agent in a worktree must hand its artifact back in its return value,
#     or write it under the main checkout resolved from the hook `cwd`.
#   - In a project where .foundry/ is gitignored entirely, a worktree starts with no
#     Foundry state at all. List the parts that must travel here, as real files.
